{
  "id": "ticket_01KYB241N9MVKZ633P4YBSK64Q",
  "name": "JSON shapes are inconsistent across the loop: start nests, stop/done/update are flat",
  "slug": "json-shapes-are-inconsistent-across",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "An agent reads ticket.id from start --json but id from done --json",
    "details_md": "Verified against the packaged binary:\n- `start --json` -> {session:{...}, ticket:{...}, git:{...}, takeover, re_entry, warnings}\n- `stop --json`  -> {id, slug, handle, name, state, note, session_id, transcript}   (FLAT)\n- `done --json`  -> {id, slug, handle, name, state, note, transcript, unblocked, problems, skipped_review, resolution_set} (FLAT)\n- `update --json`-> {id, slug, handle, name, state, priority, reparented_descendants} (FLAT)\n- `new --json`   -> {id, slug, handle, name, state, priority, parent} (FLAT)\n\nSo the ticket identity lives at `ticket.id` in one command and `id` in the next, and the session-lifecycle commands additionally mix ticket fields and session fields at the same level (`id` is the TICKET, but `session_id` is the session).\n\nProposed rule (coherent and documentable): commands that report ONLY a ticket stay flat (new/update/draft/undraft); commands that report a ticket AND a session nest as {ticket:{...}, session:{...}} plus command-specific extras (unblocked, problems, warnings) at top level — i.e. stop/done/drop/review adopt `start`'s existing shape. Breaking, but the unreleased line already carries breaking JSON/CLI changes and v0 is pre-1.0.\n\nNOT done during the fix waves because the shapes were only comparable once every command had --json; deliberately deferred rather than churned mid-flight.",
    "acceptance": [
      "One documented rule for --json shapes across every command",
      "Session-lifecycle commands (start/stop/done/drop/review) agree on ticket/session nesting",
      "docs/cli-reference.md documents the rule; CHANGELOG notes the break"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/{start,stop,done,drop,review,update,new}.ts"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
  "state": "done",
  "priority": 2,
